#
# This board always runs under MCUboot: the flash layout lives in the dts, and this is where the
# upgrade path brings what it needs. Values, not switches — an image that runs under MCUboot always manages
# images and always sets the boot-mode flag before asking for serial recovery
# (doc/08-firmware.md 6), so there is nothing here to turn off:
#
#   - stream flash + image manager: read the image state, confirm this build, roll back
#   - retention + retention boot mode: the flag the application sets and MCUboot reads to stay
#     in serial recovery across the reboot
#
# The bootloader image reads this defconfig as well. It already enables retention (Zephyr's
# MCUboot configuration); only the image manager is new for it.
CONFIG_STREAM_FLASH=y
CONFIG_IMG_MANAGER=y
CONFIG_RETAINED_MEM=y
CONFIG_RETENTION=y
CONFIG_RETENTION_BOOT_MODE=y
